<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States invasion of Panama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1989">1989</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Operation Just Cause</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> invasion of Panama, code-named Operation Just Cause, began on 20 December 1989, when about 26,000 American troops attacked to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panamanian-defense-forces">Panama Defence Forces</a> were quickly destroyed, but hundreds of Panamanians were killed, many of them civilians, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-chorrillo">El Chorrillo</a> district burned. Noriega surrendered on 3 January 1990, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillermo-endara">Guillermo Endara</a>, winner of the annulled 1989 election, became president.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states-invasion-of-panama.jpg" alt="United States invasion of Panama" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LLs; derivative work by Georgfotoart · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Operation_Just_Cause_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
